(text "Isolated supply: protected 5V -> push-pull transformer -> rectifier -> 3.3V / 1A buck" (at 20.32 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left top)) (uuid 99584d26-192c-463b-8996-728eb1491166))
(text "Design target: 0.8A combined 3.3V load, including ESP32 radio peaks, STM32 and acquisition circuits.\nC45/C46 provide 20uF nominal; 2.2uH / 20uF is within the TPS6216x recommended LC range.\nT1 is 1:1.1, with primary center tap pin 2 and isolated secondary center tap pin 5.\nUSB_GND must never connect to scoring GND. Keep primary copper out of the isolation gap on every layer.\nR79 defaults the transformer OFF. SCORING_POWER_EN must come from qualified-source AND USB-suspend policy.\nUSB_5V_PROTECTED requires input overvoltage/current protection; do not connect it directly to a PD input.\nU22 power-good holds STM32 reset low until its output is valid. R80 discharges the output when power is removed.\nBench verification remains required: low input voltage, radio load steps, temperature, shutdown and insulation." (at 20.32 177.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid 9b2b7213-3ab4-433f-8c49-9d17b8f8121d))
